    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "Allow me to interrupt for a second. If I may, Mr. Kucinich or Congressman Kucinich, there is a difference between comprehensive immigration reform and border security. This is something that is a running joke. Every time somebody asks, for example, the president's press secretary, Queen John Pierre, about border security. And we're talking about literally trying to stop the invasion as we see videos of just thousands of people flooding across our border. And she says, well, there's always, there's the president proposed comprehensive immigration reform. Well, that's different. Comprehensive immigration reform involves, well, if I may, before I finish the question, let me finish the question, comprehensive immigration reform always involves some sort of asylum or pathway to citizenship. You know, and that's a problem, not asylum. But a pathway to citizenship and amnesty is what I mean to say. For the, you know, they used to say there's 11 million illegal immigrants in this country here. Well, we've had almost that many just in the three years of Biden. So let's double it and call that a day at over 20 million people here. We would be giving amnesty to and thus, and then a pathway to citizenship. That's what the Democrats have put forth as quote unquote border security. That's not border security. Border security is about barriers. Border security is about turning people away and not welcoming them in and then saying, we'll process you and see a catch and release program. We'll see you back here in three or four years when your case comes up. So can you please clarify for me what you mean when you say you oppose this invasion, but you're all about comprehensive immigration reform?",
